Export the shape from the sizes, not through torch._shape_as_tensor.

Why: torch 2.12 (the monorepo's pin) cannot run `torch._shape_as_tensor` on the
Dynamo exporter's fake tensors ("data is not allocated yet"); upstream exports on
torch 2.13. Stacking scalar tensors of the (possibly symbolic) sizes exports the same
Shape-derived graph and keeps every dynamic axis symbolic.

Remove when: the workspace moves to torch >= 2.13 and an export of the RaCo graphs
without this patch keeps its dynamic axes (colsfm-raco-export).

--- a/lightglue_dynamo/ops/shape_utils.py
+++ b/lightglue_dynamo/ops/shape_utils.py
@@ -3,6 +3,13 @@
 
 def shape_as_tensor(tensor: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
     """Return dynamic shape as a tensor when exporting; otherwise use eager shape."""
-    if torch.onnx.is_in_onnx_export() and hasattr(torch, "_shape_as_tensor"):
-        return torch._shape_as_tensor(tensor)
+    if torch.onnx.is_in_onnx_export():
+        return torch.stack(
+            [
+                torch.tensor(size, dtype=torch.int64, device=tensor.device)
+                if isinstance(size, int)
+                else torch.scalar_tensor(size, dtype=torch.int64, device=tensor.device)
+                for size in tensor.shape
+            ]
+        )
     return torch.tensor(tensor.shape, device=tensor.device)
